From tru64-unix-managers  Wed Jan 27 15:33:20 1999
From: Toni Harbaugh-Blackford <harbaugh () ncifcrf ! gov>
Date: Wed, 27 Jan 1999 15:33:20 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: [SUMMARY] netstat command fails with 'no namelist' error
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96079034715888

Folks-

Several people responded, suggesting that I might have rebuilt the
kernel so that the running kernel did not match the one on disk.
However, this was not the case.

I called DEC support, and they provided the answer.
It turns out that 'netstat' depends on the 'kloadsrv' process, which
had died on our system.  Restarting the process with the command

   /sbin/kloadsrv

fixed the problem.

Thanks to all those who responded.

Toni

