I had asked where HSZterm is found and what the package name is.  The
question was in relation to Digital Unix 4.0D.

I'll be verifying this probably later today, but in the meantime here's
what I was told:

Thanks to:

Roger Picard, Allan Simeone, Steven Nash, Randy Cable, Alexander
Sakellaris, Alan Rollow, Bruce Kelly, Randy Rogers

CD Title:	Software Product Library CD #3
Location:	/swa11a
Package Name:   SWACLI11A
Package Title:  HSZ40 Array Controller Utility

Also, there are two additional packages I was told about:

Package Name:	SWADOC11A (Documentation?)
Package Name:	SWAMAN11A (Man Pages?)

One response indicates that HSZTerm is NOT Y2K complaint and therefore
should no loger be used.  I have not verified this.

Another respondant indicated to use the new "Command Console" GUI that
runs on Windows machines.  (We had the OLD version 1.1 but it never
installed properly.)  The new version 2.0 is publicly available.  We
will probably attempt to install that today or tommorow:

http://www.storage.digital.com/swrks/homepage/support/swcc/index.htm

