What a pain. Finally found out my problem. It was with
the init code that dip was sending to the modem. (linux end)

Now what I need to do is:

dip -t
dip>get $remote ip
dip>get $local ip
dip>port /dev/ttyS0
dip>speed 19200
dip>term

Now give the modem the commands to dial the # manually
escape out of term.

dip>mode slip

Now it works ok.

what a PIA.

George Gallen
ggallen@slackinc.com

