Hello alphas,
new things to learn every day ;-)

my original question was:

> Hello,
> as i saw, the "scsimgr" utility is envoke on each startup 
> sind DU4.0.
> So, after adding a controller to the system - let's say a 
> KZPSA-BB, do i
> have to do a kernel rebuild or not?
> 

the answer is (thank you Drs Blinn and Luchini):
every time a new bus or controller is to be added to the system, you
have to run a kernel build. This won't change in DU 4.0x (perhaps
later). Everything the "scsimgr" utility does, is to find new devices on
a given bus!



