To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY : rc files
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96079034715663

Question:

> What permissions are needed on the rc files (rc0, rc2, etc.)?  Can I set
> them to 750?

Thanks to Dr. Tom Blinn, I found out quickly that:

While it is possible to change the file permissions on these files, there
is no obvious need to do so as the scripts check for superuser as default.  

Note: these files have protections recorded in the inv files in /usr/.smdb.
and any changes you make to the protections are likely to impact your
ability to patch or update your system unless you also change the inventory
records; even if you do change the inventory records to match what you set
as protections on the files, they will get reset to the current set of
protections during a system update installation.

Thanks, Tom!!

-Adrian Cole
Hood College

