Hi DU Admins

The problem was that I wasn't able to mount 2 of a group of CDs I 
recently burnt on some alphas even though I could mount them on a PC, 
a Mac and on some older alphas running DU.

Thanks to Jason Xu, Marie-Claude Vialatte, Gary George, 
Serguei Patchkovskii and Cory Erickson for their replies.

Suggestions ranged over: was I using the correct device?;  is the
CDFS option in the kernel config?; were the CDs burnt in the
correct format?; was I using the correct mount options?

The answer to all these is yes proven by the fact that I can
mount all the other CDs that I burnt without problem and
I can mount the two problem CDs under other OS's and also
on other alphas running DU.

Here's the evidence:

   It's only 2 out of 10 disks that cause problems.

   I can read them under NT, on a Mac, and on some alphas running DU.

   They're both copies of the same data set - the largest data set.

   They're both perfect copies: verified on an alpha where I could 
   mount them.
   
The most interesting reply came from Serguei who said:

> Are these disks per chance recorded in several sessions? At least
> some CD-ROMs shipped with DPWs (well, all DPWs *we* have) have a
> trouble reading multisession CDs even after they were properly
> closed. 

They were recorded in one session so that's not the problem but maybe 
it's related since it's the au series PWSs that give trouble.  I also 
couldn't mount the problem disks on an AlphaStation 200 4/233.

I still suspect it's the size of the data set that's the problem.  
I'm going to stay below 550MB from now on.


Regards
Ian

